# LINE ENDINGS: LF ALWAYS, including in the working copy on Windows.
#
# Not a style preference. `image/cont-init.d/*` and `image/s6-overlay/**` are
# shell scripts run INSIDE the Linux container. With CRLF the interpreter reads
# the `\r` as part of the command and the script dies -- at boot, after the
# build, far from whoever edited it.
#
# Without this line git on Windows converts on checkout ("LF will be replaced by
# CRLF the next time Git touches it") and the next build carries the broken
# scripts into the image.
* text=auto eol=lf
